{"name":"Lyrebird","hex":"#0087ad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lyrebird","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Either of two large ground-dwelling Australian songbirds, of the genus Menura, notable for their extraordinary ability to mimic natural and artificial sounds from their environment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lyrebird"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lyrebird","blocks":[{"text":"A lyrebird is either of two species of ground-dwelling Australian birds that compose the genus Menura, and the family Menuridae. They are most notable for their ability to mimic a variety of natural and artificial sounds from their environment and for the striking beauty of the male bird's huge tail when it is fanned out in courtship display. Lyrebirds have unique plumes of neutral-coloured tailfeathers and are among Australia's best-known native birds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Superb_lyrbird_in_scrub.jpg/330px-Superb_lyrbird_in_scrub.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyrebird","wikidata":"Q214096"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Menura_superba_-_Thomas_Davies.jpg/500px-Menura_superba_-_Thomas_Davies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Menura_superba_-_Thomas_Davies.jpg/1280px-Menura_superba_-_Thomas_Davies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Menura_superba_-_Thomas_Davies.jpg/500px-Menura_superba_-_Thomas_Davies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Menura novaehollandiae – superb lyrebird (1800) by Thomas Davies","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMenura_superba_-_Thomas_Davies.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wik